{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/61389-question-on-a-potential-hunter-chronicle","id":61389,"title":"Question on a potential Hunter Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-30T01:39:11-08:00","id":61389,"title":"Question on a potential Hunter Chronicle","content":"<br /> <br /> I remember when Vigil came out and it was said more than once* that Hunter could easily be the WoD core really, or at least just a natural extension to it.<br /> <br /> Now I love the rules update and GMC in general but I'm wondering about further blue books and whether or not they are going to focus more on the God-Machine than anything else**.<br /> <br /> If there was a Hunter Chronicle it's still going to be about investigating and battling against the supernatural in general, even if you may happen to begin with mortals who know about supernaturals to some extent from the start.***<br /> <br /> To that end, would you consider that a Hunter: the Vigil Chronicle book, with the GMC update and core WoD rules (aka B&amp;S) within to be more of a World of Darkness 2.0 than using the rules update (wherever you're using it from) with the original blue book? - especially because you're likely to have updated mortal characters within as NPC's using the rules update as well as non-god-machine supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and You're Wrong Buddy arguments welcome.<br /> <br /> *citation and further explanation needed<br /> **lets say for sake of argument that they are, irrelevant to whether they actually will be for purposes of this question.<br /> ***and a hunter's knowledge of supernaturals are not often indepth","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T02:45:14-08:00","id":61411,"title":"","content":"I suppose it kinda would be. Not sure of the significance of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T02:55:32-08:00","id":61417,"title":"","content":"Well quite a few folk wanted a full, new WoD 2.0 book.<br /> <br /> I find that it's a lot easier to go over the rules in Blood and Smoke, which contain all the rules and GMC update, then I do flipping between the Update and the WoD core blue book.<br /> <br /> Hunter would have everything rules-wise in, be centered on Humans and General-Supernaturals - which I think would be quite significant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T16:59:26-08:00","id":61835,"title":"","content":"It would have to be more a little comprehensive than blood and smokes though, Hunter needs the ghost and spirit rules, where vampire doesn't. But yeah there isn't a huge amount of difference between tier 1 Hunters and mortals. <br /> <br /> Although honestly the old nWoD core book is something I bring along for character generation, and between character gen sessions it's only really been used in a really technical problem on Willpower expenditure. (It occasionally comes up in our vampire game but that's only because it's the only game I have played in for years that actually uses the virtue/vice system) Now Mirrors on the other hand occasionally gets used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/711-mcgonigle","name":"mcgonigle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T18:57:27-08:00","id":61918,"title":"","content":"Since I picked up Hunter, I've used it in non-hunter games just as often as I've used the blue book. Dread Powers, and the whole custom monster building system is incredibly useful for any game, when you don't want to drag the baggage of, say, the Forsaken, but you still want werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T18:55:07-08:00","id":63213,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Mortal Remains is going to be the equivalent of a Chronicle book, updating Hunters to the GMC rules, but not forcing it to be about the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T08:45:36-08:00","id":63453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/61389-question-on-a-potential-hunter-chronicle?p=63213#post63213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Mortal Remains is going to be the equivalent of a Chronicle book, updating Hunters to the GMC rules, but not forcing it to be about the God Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...yes and no<br /> <br /> It'll update it rules wise as in as much as you still will need WoD blue book, Hunter and Mortal Remains. - But it's also about how Hunter's fight specific splats not yet covered.<br /> <br /> If there was later on a full Chronicle book that contained all the rules needed for play, had the great (but updated) system for creating any monsters - inc god-machine ones I guess, but not <i>only</i> - with perhaps a specific hunter-centric villain, then it would, for my money, be as near as a full one book WoD 2.0 as we'd get. It's worth remembering that the Chronicle Books are not based around the god-machine, they just have the GMC rules update in them - and if they follow Blood and Smoke they have the truncated rules in them too.<br /> <br /> At least for a couple of years until WoD 2.0 will ultimately get a release* (although it might not even be GoD-Machine dependent then).<br /> <br /> Ideally, for me I'd really like to see all of the books get a Chronicle treatment - even Mummy and Demon: the Decent. And then a WoD 2.0 (but that's only because I've got to grips with the rules now...mainly after Blood and Smoke came out and I didn't have to flip through books.<br /> <br /> *yeah, it's speculation, but years ago I said they would release another edition of Vampire the Masquerade, and they all laughed at me then too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","user":"MeetsInTaverns","date":". 02-02-2014, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T17:45:08-08:00","id":63665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/61389-question-on-a-potential-hunter-chronicle?p=63213#post63213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Mortal Remains is going to be the equivalent of a Chronicle book, updating Hunters to the GMC rules, but not forcing it to be about the God Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was kinda a V.1.0 book with notes on updating the mechanics to v2.0 but not a full on 2.0 book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>in any fight<br /> it is the guy who is willing to die<br /> who is going to win that inch.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1402-kael-winters","name":"Kael Winters","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T18:19:19-08:00","id":63672,"title":"","content":"There's not many rules that need to be changed. The basic combat and merit changes have been available for free in the God Machine rules system.<br /> Mortal Remains will have updated rules to bring the game into GMC level stuff.<br /> I can't see what kind of chronicle book they'd need, if all the rules are already updated via Mortal Remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T00:52:59-08:00","id":63819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/61389-question-on-a-potential-hunter-chronicle?p=63672#post63672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not many rules that need to be changed. The basic combat and merit changes have been available for free in the God Machine rules system.<br /> Mortal Remains will have updated rules to bring the game into GMC level stuff.<br /> I can't see what kind of chronicle book they'd need, if all the rules are already updated via Mortal Remains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, it's all speculation really on my part but I would think that not all the rules could be updated, especially as chunks of the book would be taken up with how to deal with mummies etc.<br /> <br /> I would still think that a Hunter Chronicle could be magnificent as a chronicle book and as a WoD 2.0. After all the Hunter's can easily have other hunters as the enemy depending on what tier you're playing and a massive set of dread powers at the back designed to make any kind of super you want.<br /> <br /> I guess my big point, is that a lot of folk lament the fact that CCP didn't approve a WoD. 2.0 core book and that's why there's updates. Blood and Smoke (and hopefully future chronicle books) have all of the rules in including the update. As a set of chronicle books they would constitute WoD 2.0 and if there was a hunter one it could really focus on the mortal, the hunter and the threat of the supernatural unknown without having to look at specific types of supernatural as a central focus. After all, most of what makes playing a mortal scary is the fact you're fighting/investigating something you don't know a lot about. If there were to be a stock enemy in the chronicle (that wasn't a competing hunter group - which I'd go for completely - it wouldn't be vital and necessarily to running that game, after all I quite like the Strix as occasional enemies, but I'm not going to run Blood and Smoke as a Strix centric game (the beauty of the way the game is set up allows this)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T05:42:45-08:00","id":63897,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't really like a WoD 2.0 based on hunter. For me mortal chronicles are about investigation of supernatural weirdness and not about hunting the supernatural. Incorporating the hunter themes into a new core book would thus feel constraining to me. The supernatural should not be portrayed as antagonistic by default, as it often is portrayed in hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T04:59:31-08:00","id":64750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/61389-question-on-a-potential-hunter-chronicle?p=63897#post63897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't really like a WoD 2.0 based on hunter. For me mortal chronicles are about investigation of supernatural weirdness and not about hunting the supernatural. Incorporating the hunter themes into a new core book would thus feel constraining to me. The supernatural should not be portrayed as antagonistic by default, as it often is portrayed in hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Network 0, Null Mysteries, Loyalist of Thule are all set to have a less antagonistic base setting with the supernatural, all three are a good so you have a good reason to go out and look for the supernatural, and you could run a campaign for all of them that doesn't involve violence. Then you have the huge number of 'Defensive groups' all of which have plot hooks which basically revolve around - okay this has turned up, is it a threat? And if you want to run something more conciliatory with the supernatural many of the hunter organisations make amazing bad guys, so you have spent the last few sessions helping the teenage werewolf create coping strategies and suddenly this strange group of scientists with white vans is asking questions about him, quoting EEC regulations.<br /> <br /> Hell I used Hunter to run a game where the players essentially ended up playing Councillors for the supernatural. The reason hunter is regarded as the replacement core, is the rules are strongly set up to encourage uncertainty, tricks to allow the GM to make the players as clueless as their characters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/711-mcgonigle","name":"mcgonigle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T07:44:22-08:00","id":64831,"title":"","content":"I agree with you about the groups. It is some of the rules I don't like. My greatest problem is with the concept of Vigil. In my opinion the book often tries to shoehorn ways mortals react to the supernatural into this concept. Not every mortal who knows about the supernatural needs to be this wary and go hunt the unseen to protect others (or do it just for kicks). Under the Risking Willpower rules they even generalize that hunters have a bloody-minded focus.<br /> <br /> I just don't like this part of the hunter themes. But luckily a lot of hunter (including many organisations) are not built on this theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}